Procedure and Measurements. First, the leading investigator briefed participants and asked for their informed consent. The study then started with Task A (intervention) tutorial and participants got a quick introduction to the driving simulator, and we explained the necessary commands. Further, they drove a tutorial track to overtake trucks (lane-change maneuvers) to get comfortable with the different control modalities. Afterwards, each participant experienced five experimental conditions (same route) in a counterbalanced within-subject design. In each condition, the leading investigator began with standardized instructions to introduce Task B. Then, he left the scene or acted in the conditions "Eating" and "Talking" as a co-passenger. During the non-driving-related activities (Task B), participants intervened four times (see Task A) in the autonomously driving cars’ behavior (operated by the system wizard). Participants had the free choice to execute these maneu
